[Desktop Entry]
Type=Application
Name=Calculator
GenericName=Calculator
Comment=A calculator on nitro-ui
# The file name is `nitro-calc.desktop` and the application's app id is
# `nitro-calc` — the same string, deliberately. `nitro-bar`'s window list
# resolves an icon by using a window's app id *as* an icon name
# (docs/shell.md), which is the freedesktop convention and works exactly
# when the two agree. Renaming either without the other silently costs
# the bar its icon.
#
# `Icon=` names one of the **server's own symbolic icons**, not an icon
# theme's: nitro's apps ship no artwork of their own, and a shape from
# the compiled-in set is present on every box including one with no icon
# theme installed at all. The launcher's built-in entry names the same
# shape, so a box with this file and a box without look the same.
#
# That last sentence is true **because the launcher asks for the app
# id**, not for this `Icon=` value — and it was briefly false during
# #3723, which is why it is spelled out here. A row that sent
# `calculator` with the coloured role would reach the icon *theme*, which
# has no such file on our boxes, and fall back to the generic `window`;
# sending `nitro-calc` lets the server take the same `<app_id>.desktop`
# hop it takes for the bar and land back on this line.
# `crates/nitro-launcher/src/lib.rs`'s `row_icon` has the argument.
#
# `just deploy` installs this file into `~/.local/share/applications` on
# the test box (#3723), and it is a bare `Exec=` on purpose: see
# `nitro-term.desktop` for why that now resolves there as well as on a
# system where the binary is in `/usr/bin`.
Exec=nitro-calc
Icon=calculator
Terminal=false
StartupWMClass=nitro-calc
Categories=Utility;Calculator;
Keywords=calculator;maths;arithmetic;
